{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Snowplow’s tracker protocol, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to a Snowplow collector’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":", as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-describing events whose schemas are the tracking plan’s."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"title":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SnowplowBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder.swift#L93"},"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fills in the endpoint, the header field that keeps the collector from setting a cookie or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recording the request’s address, this encoder and its limits:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your schemas' Iglu vendor","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a self-describing JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", of the schema"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/payload_data\/jsonschema\/1-0-4"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data"},{"type":"text","text":" is an array of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events, one per record, oldest first. Every member of an event is a string, as the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol has them:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The app ID the encoder is made with","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context’s entities (below), as the text of a self-describing JSON array of "},{"code":"contexts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out when there are none"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in epoch milliseconds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a self-describing event","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID; a redelivered record keeps it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The platform: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone, pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" when the record has no device in its context"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID; left out when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traffluent"},{"text":", the tracker","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ue_pr","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event, as the text of a self-describing JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"unstruct_event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holding the event’s own self-describing JSON: its schema, ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its data, its stored properties by name","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nuid"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tnuid"},{"type":"text","text":", no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_session"},{"type":"text","text":" entity, whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":" lasts across sessions, and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appleIdfv"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appleIdfa"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or other device identifier. Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"domain_sessionid"},{"type":"text","text":" is the session; a record with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store recovered after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a relaunch, which keeps no context) is sent without one, linked to nothing. The record’s vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", its true timestamp, is the record’s timestamp, as is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":", so Snowplow’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when the event was tracked, uncorrected for the device’s clock. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s schema is named after its "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Event\/schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": version N is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SchemaVer "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each version of an event is a breaking change, a SchemaVer MODEL. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compatible change at the same version is an ADDITION, which the tracking plan’s Iglu export"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") writes for Iglu Server as "},{"code":"N-0-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on, each superseding the ones before, so an event naming "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is validated against the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newest of them. A static repository doesn’t supersede: there an event naming "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated against "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone, so the export refuses an addition for one, and a change to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event needs a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data then validates against the event’s exported schema, which never requires a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds these entities, for the keys the record’s context has values for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/mobile_context\/jsonschema\/1-0-3"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", both; "},{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if present"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"osType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"ios","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tvos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"watchos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"visionos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"osx","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"osVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceManufacturer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Apple Inc.","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"networkType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"mobile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"offline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; left out for a wired or other connection); ","type":"text"},{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the locale’s language code","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.mobile\/application\/jsonschema\/1-0-0","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"},{"text":", with both a version and a build","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Iglu doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"take, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is outside the years 0 to 9999, and one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. The collector answers 200 to every request it can read, and Snowplow validates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the events afterwards: an event whose data its schema rejects, or whose schema the pipeline’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, becomes a failed event, kept apart from the warehouse, though the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination counts it as delivered. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/transientStatuses":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transientStatuses"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":